572
00:34:06,220 --> 00:34:09,500
One very famous booby-trap case involved a gambling casino

573
00:34:09,501 --> 00:34:12,640
in a small Nevada town called Stateline.

574
00:34:12,740 --> 00:34:14,500
The year was 1981.

575
00:34:14,600 --> 00:34:15,740
They made this big bomb.

576
00:34:15,840 --> 00:34:17,640
They put it in the Harveys Casino.

577
00:34:17,740 --> 00:34:19,140
They said, you give us some money,

578
00:34:19,240 --> 00:34:20,540
and we'll tell you how to take it apart.

579
00:34:20,640 --> 00:34:22,440
Classic extortion bombing.

580
00:34:22,540 --> 00:34:25,940
The extortionists had built 25 tamper-proof booby-trap

581
00:34:26,040 --> 00:34:29,160
devices inside a refrigerator bomb.

582
00:34:29,260 --> 00:34:32,760
Authorities decided it would be safer to destroy the 1,100-pound

583
00:34:32,860 --> 00:34:35,860
bomb in place rather than risk trying to disarm it.

584
00:34:39,500 --> 00:34:44,500
There is another disturbing development

585
00:34:44,600 --> 00:34:46,500
in the use of booby traps.

586
00:34:46,600 --> 00:34:49,500
Otherwise law-abiding citizens are using them

587
00:34:49,600 --> 00:34:51,740
to take the law into their own hands.

588
00:34:51,840 --> 00:34:54,940
We see private citizens, store owners,

589
00:34:55,040 --> 00:34:57,260
setting up their own form of booby traps

590
00:34:57,360 --> 00:34:59,360
to protect themselves, their property.

591
00:34:59,460 --> 00:35:02,260
So when the burglar breaks into the back of a store

592
00:35:02,360 --> 00:35:06,260
at night again, that shotgun is there to face him.

593
00:35:06,261 --> 00:35:08,400
that shotgun is there to face him.

594
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:10,640
Of course, that's illegal.

595
00:35:12,500 --> 00:35:15,900
A classic case occurred in 1990 in Denver, Colorado.

596
00:35:17,240 --> 00:35:19,980
A warehouse owner, tired of frequent break-ins,

597
00:35:20,600 --> 00:35:23,120
rigged a 12-gauge shotgun booby trap to a window.

598
00:35:23,920 --> 00:35:25,500
When a teenage burglar was killed,

599
00:35:26,020 --> 00:35:28,840
the businessman was tried and convicted of manslaughter.

600
00:35:29,520 --> 00:35:31,260
I was just pushed too far.

601
00:35:31,800 --> 00:35:33,320
They were stealing my life.

602
00:35:33,640 --> 00:35:34,600
It was like a war.

603
00:35:34,601 --> 00:35:38,000
I mean, it was either it was my survival that I was trying to

604
00:35:38,001 --> 00:35:41,900
protect. And then the booby trap

605
00:35:41,901 --> 00:35:46,140
maker lost a wrongful death lawsuit brought by the dead

606
00:35:46,141 --> 00:35:52,920
thief's family. On April 23, 1978, mobster

607
00:35:52,921 --> 00:35:56,980
Salvador Gingillo, better known as Sammy G, got into his car

608
00:35:56,981 --> 00:36:00,160
outside a cafe in Rochester, New York, and turned on the key.

609
00:36:00,161 --> 00:36:04,460
The car blew sky high, killing Sammy and seriously injuring

610
00:36:04,560 --> 00:36:06,700
his two bodyguards.

611
00:36:06,800 --> 00:36:11,500
Then FBI agent Clint Van Zandt was called to the scene.

612
00:36:11,600 --> 00:36:15,300
The drunks, the winos, the pimps, the prostitutes

613
00:36:15,400 --> 00:36:17,380
that had been standing around watching

614
00:36:17,480 --> 00:36:20,880
ran over and started picking up the pieces of metal,

615
00:36:20,980 --> 00:36:22,380
the shards of glass.

616
00:36:22,480 --> 00:36:27,820
They all wanted a souvenir of the demise of Sammy G.

617
00:36:27,821 --> 00:36:30,320
Gangsters have been booby-trapping the cars of the

618
00:36:30,321 --> 00:36:33,320
competition with bombs ever since crime became an organized

619
00:36:33,321 --> 00:36:37,820
business. But an alarming number of public

620
00:36:37,821 --> 00:36:40,820
officials and corporate executives in the U.S. and abroad

621
00:36:40,821 --> 00:36:45,820
have found they, too, are targets for car bombs.

622
00:36:45,821 --> 00:36:48,820
The increased demand for corporate security has spawned a

623
00:36:48,821 --> 00:36:52,820
new industry, the under-vehicle booby-trap detector.

624
00:36:52,821 --> 00:36:55,820
Because the designs are proprietary, no pictures of the

625
00:36:55,821 --> 00:36:59,560
No pictures of the devices are available.

626
00:36:59,660 --> 00:37:01,760
Basically, it works like this.

627
00:37:01,860 --> 00:37:05,020
If a bomb is attached to the car's frame with magnets,

628
00:37:05,120 --> 00:37:09,760
the detector will sense it immediately.

629
00:37:09,860 --> 00:37:12,780
Ever since the anthrax mail scare in 2001,

630
00:37:12,880 --> 00:37:15,380
even ordinary citizens are becoming fearful of this new

631
00:37:15,480 --> 00:37:20,380
brand of booby trap.

632
00:37:20,480 --> 00:37:23,480
The portable letter bomb detector detects known agencies

633
00:37:23,481 --> 00:37:27,480
of bomb-making material like Syntex, C4,

634
00:37:27,481 --> 00:37:30,480
ammonium nitrate, TNT.

635
00:37:30,481 --> 00:37:34,480
The device allows the user to pass unopened mail

636
00:37:34,481 --> 00:37:37,480
across the target zone where the crosshairs are.

637
00:37:37,481 --> 00:37:41,480
If the letter is laced with any explosive material,

638
00:37:41,481 --> 00:37:44,480
the device will go off.

639
00:37:47,480 --> 00:37:49,480
Not all booby traps are deadly,

640
00:37:49,481 --> 00:37:52,480
but there are some out there that cause a lot of suffering.

641
00:37:52,481 --> 00:37:57,480
computer viruses. These treacherous cyber thugs

642
00:37:57,580 --> 00:38:02,120
qualify as booby traps. They engage an unsuspecting victim

643
00:38:02,220 --> 00:38:07,220
with an invitation to open seemingly harmless e-mail.

644
00:38:07,320 --> 00:38:10,140
The result of following their simple instructions could

645
00:38:10,240 --> 00:38:12,640
ultimately lead to the destruction of irreplaceable

646
00:38:12,740 --> 00:38:16,980
data. In 1985, there were 11 known

647
00:38:17,080 --> 00:38:21,680
viruses. Today, there are over 60,000.

648
00:38:21,681 --> 00:38:24,680
The success of these cyber traps is often based on the public's

649
00:38:24,681 --> 00:38:28,480
desire for freebies. Computer booby traps are

650
00:38:28,481 --> 00:38:33,520
something which lure a user into a false sense of security with

651
00:38:33,521 --> 00:38:37,520
the promise of some sort of reward and at the end ends up

652
00:38:37,521 --> 00:38:41,840
tricking them in some way and giving them something unexpected.

653
00:38:41,841 --> 00:38:45,480
That unexpected surprise is often a virus.

654
00:38:45,481 --> 00:38:48,480
They end up triggering a mechanism which usually causes

655
00:38:48,481 --> 00:38:51,720
damage or further propagates the virus.

656
00:38:51,820 --> 00:38:54,880
The lure of the freebie has produced a multimillion-dollar

657
00:38:54,980 --> 00:38:57,020
antivirus industry.

658
00:38:57,120 --> 00:39:01,420
The question is, do these antivirus programs really work?

659
00:39:01,520 --> 00:39:05,440
There are probably 30 to 100 new viruses every month.

660
00:39:05,540 --> 00:39:08,840
So you can sort of do the math, figure one to three a day.

661
00:39:08,940 --> 00:39:12,140
So if you're updating every day, you seriously cut down the risk

662
00:39:12,240 --> 00:39:14,140
that you're going to be infected with a virus.

663
00:39:14,240 --> 00:39:16,840
And I say cut down, something new is going to hit your system,

664
00:39:16,841 --> 00:39:21,440
system, and until we figure out a way that doesn't rely on

665
00:39:21,441 --> 00:39:24,280
catching up with the viruses as they're written, we're always

666
00:39:24,281 --> 00:39:26,440
going to be one step behind.

667
00:39:26,441 --> 00:39:29,280
While we may be a step behind computer viruses,

668
00:39:29,281 --> 00:39:33,480
software designers are staying a step ahead of software thieves.

669
00:39:33,481 --> 00:39:36,840
Probably the most interesting example of this is the latest

670
00:39:36,841 --> 00:39:39,960
incarnation of the Windows operating system, Windows XP,

671
00:39:39,961 --> 00:39:42,440
which actually needs an activation code which is

672
00:39:42,441 --> 00:39:44,800
checked periodically back at Microsoft.

673
00:39:44,801 --> 00:39:47,100
If too many things on the system are changed,

674
00:39:47,200 --> 00:39:51,100
